      "id": 4,
      "kind": "mother_usage",
      "payload": "{\"model_calls\":1,\"phase\":\"preparation\",\"plan\":{\"A\":\"Explore a conservative OpenMP baseline: parallelize the outer body loop in force calculation with static scheduling, and parallelize the independent position-update loop. Keep each body's inner j loop serial and in increasing order, with a barrier before position updates. Preserve the original arithmetic and verify output correctness; measure the complete program, not just the kernel.\",\"B\":\"Explore keeping one OpenMP team alive across all 10 simulation steps to reduce repeated fork/join overhead. Use worksharing for the force and position-update loops, retaining the necessary barriers between them and the original serial j order and arithmetic for each body. Compare end-to-end timing and correctness against the baseline and A's candidate.\",\"C\":\"Explore ARM64 SIMD batching of inner-loop pair calculations, while retaining each body's contributions and accumulation in the original increasing-j order. Preserve the original float/double conversions and operation order, including the double-precision sqrt call; do not use reassociation or approximate math. Verify correctness and measure end-to-end performance; reject the approach if exact semantics cannot be maintained or it does not improve runtime.\",\"G\":\"When candidates arrive, assess each independently against the valid baseline, then test any proposed combination as a complete program rather than assuming gains add. Require correctness on the available suite and review that the implementation remains generic and preserves the reference computation. Compare repeated end-to-end measurements with the baseline mean of 0.66614 seconds; select the fastest valid measured candidate, or retain the baseline if none is better. No child results or interaction measurements are available yet.\",\"analysis\":\"The run is the N-body problem on a 4-core ARM64 target with no GPUs. The baseline is valid on 4 cases, with three measured times averaging 0.66614 seconds and score 0.5. The dominant work is 10 iterations of an all-pairs force calculation. Parallelizing independent bodies offers a direct CPU opportunity; a persistent team separately targets parallel-region overhead. SIMD is a distinct exploratory path, but preserving the reference's per-body accumulation order and floating-point semantics is important for correctness. No other candidate measurements are available, so integration gains must be measured rather than inferred.\"},\"request_sha256\":\"b48747ee4498ece7d07f3dc31bdd2bd1ade1f1f43301a2234908103588c986d8\",\"response\":{\"data\":{\"A\":\"Explore a conservative OpenMP baseline: parallelize the outer body loop in force calculation with static scheduling, and parallelize the independent position-update loop. Keep each body's inner j loop serial and in increasing order, with a barrier before position updates. Preserve the original arithmetic and verify output correctness; measure the complete program, not just the kernel.\",\"B\":\"Explore keeping one OpenMP team alive across all 10 simulation steps to reduce repeated fork/join overhead. Use worksharing for the force and position-update loops, retaining the necessary barriers between them and the original serial j order and arithmetic for each body. Compare end-to-end timing and correctness against the baseline and A's candidate.\",\"C\":\"Explore ARM64 SIMD batching of inner-loop pair calculations, while retaining each body's contributions and accumulation in the original increasing-j order. Preserve the original float/double conversions and operation order, including the double-precision sqrt call; do not use reassociation or approximate math. Verify correctness and measure end-to-end performance; reject the approach if exact semantics cannot be maintained or it does not improve runtime.\",\"G\":\"When candidates arrive, assess each independently against the valid baseline, then test any proposed combination as a complete program rather than assuming gains add. Require correctness on the available suite and review that the implementation remains generic and preserves the reference computation. Compare repeated end-to-end measurements with the baseline mean of 0.66614 seconds; select the fastest valid measured candidate, or retain the baseline if none is better. No child results or interaction measurements are available yet.\",\"analysis\":\"The run is the N-body problem on a 4-core ARM64 target with no GPUs. The baseline is valid on 4 cases, with three measured times averaging 0.66614 seconds and score 0.5. The dominant work is 10 iterations of an all-pairs force calculation. Parallelizing independent bodies offers a direct CPU opportunity; a persistent team separately targets parallel-region overhead. SIMD is a distinct exploratory path, but preserving the reference's per-body accumulation order and floating-point semantics is important for correctness. No other candidate measurements are available, so integration gains must be measured rather than inferred.\"},\"error\":null,\"infrastructure_error\":false,\"model\":\"gpt-6-luna\",\"nonce\":\"ff50266ba4704340a8abf2238e8ebab4\",\"protocol\":\"hpc-forest-codex-mailbox-v1\",\"reasoning_effort\":\"xhigh\",\"request_sha256\":\"b48747ee4498ece7d07f3dc31bdd2bd1ade1f1f43301a2234908103588c986d8\",\"session_id\":\"fb704484f3a5459ca3a4a358d2208a0b\",\"usage\":{\"cached_tokens_included_in_input\":true,\"codex_jsonl_sha256\":\"dfa413a7554bb2cf46d598a2544836698da1df5b8f04a29e1bee2d7eb01372f9\",\"events\":[{\"cache_write_input_tokens\":0,\"cached_input_tokens\":0,\"input_tokens\":10415,\"output_tokens\":5591,\"reasoning_output_tokens\":5145}],\"llm_calls\":1,\"model_requested\":\"gpt-6-luna\",\"reasoning_effort_requested\":\"xhigh\",\"token_accounting\":\"exact\",\"tokens\":16006,\"tool_events\":[]}},\"status\":\"complete\"}",
